#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:1
msgid "Dummy Store"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:3
msgid "**Store URL format**: `dummy://`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:5
msgid ""
"This store type represents a store in memory. Store objects can be read and "
"written, but only so long as the store is open. Once the store is closed, "
"all data will be discarded."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:9
msgid ""
"It's useful when you want to use the Nix evaluator when no actual Nix store "
"exists, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:11
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"# nix eval --store dummy:// --expr '1 + 2'\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:15
msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:17
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-dummy-store-path-info-cache-size\">[`path-info-cache-size`]"
"(#store-dummy-store-path-info-cache-size)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:19
msgid "Size of the in-memory store path metadata cache."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:21
msgid "**Default:** `65536`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:23
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-dummy-store-priority\">[`priority`](#store-dummy-store-"
"priority)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:25
msgid ""
"Priority of this store when used as a [substituter](../../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-substituters). A lower value means a higher priority."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:28
msgid "**Default:** `0`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:30
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-dummy-store-read-only\">[`read-only`](#store-dummy-store-"
"read-only)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:32
msgid ""
"Make any sort of write fail instead of succeeding. No additional memory will "
"be used, because no information needs to be stored."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:35
msgid "**Default:** `true`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:37
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-dummy-store-store\">[`store`](#store-dummy-store-store)</"
"span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:39
msgid "Logical location of the Nix store, usually `/nix/store`."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:41
msgid ""
"Defaults to [`NIX_STORE_DIR`](../../command-ref/env-common.md#env-"
"NIX_STORE_DIR) if unset."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:43
msgid ""
"Note that you can only copy store paths between stores if they have the same "
"`store` setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:45
msgid "**Default:** `/nix/store`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:47
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-dummy-store-system-features\">[`system-features`](#store-"
"dummy-store-system-features)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:49
msgid ""
"Optional [system features](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-system-"
"features) available on the system this store uses to build derivations."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:51
msgid "Example: `\"kvm\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:53
msgid "**Default:** _machine-specific_"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:55
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-dummy-store-trusted\">[`trusted`](#store-dummy-store-"
"trusted)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:57
msgid ""
"Whether paths from this store can be used as substitutes even if they are "
"not signed by a key listed in the [`trusted-public-keys`](../../command-ref/"
"conf-file.md#conf-trusted-public-keys) setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:62 source/store/types/dummy-store.md:68
msgid "**Default:** `false`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:64
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-dummy-store-want-mass-query\">[`want-mass-query`](#store-"
"dummy-store-want-mass-query)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/dummy-store.md:66
msgid ""
"Whether this store can be queried efficiently for path validity when used as "
"a [substituter](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-substituters)."
msgstr ""
